<figure class="standard-diagram">
  <svg
    xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"
    viewBox="0 0 960 320"
    role="img"
    aria-labelledby="rdr-conformance-title rdr-conformance-desc"
  >
    <title id="rdr-conformance-title">
      The four conformance levels as a ladder
    </title>
    <desc id="rdr-conformance-desc">
      Four ascending steps. Level 0 emitting, level 1 append-only, level 2
      dependent, and level 3 contestable. Each step names what it adds to the
      one below it.
    </desc>

    <style>
      .ink {
        fill: var(--text, #1f2937);
      }
      .muted {
        fill: var(--muted, #6b7280);
      }
      .line {
        stroke: var(--border, #374151);
        stroke-width: 2;
        fill: none;
        stroke-linecap: round;
        stroke-linejoin: round;
      }
      .dash {
        stroke-dasharray: 6 6;
      }
      .chip {
        fill: var(--surface, #ffffff);
        stroke: var(--border, #374151);
        stroke-width: 2;
      }
      .chip-state {
        rx: 10;
        ry: 10;
      }
      .small {
        font:
          500 11px ui-sans-serif,
          system-ui,
          -apple-system,
          Segoe UI,
          Roboto;
      }
      .label {
        font:
          600 12.5px ui-sans-serif,
          system-ui,
          -apple-system,
          Segoe UI,
          Roboto;
      }
      .title {
        font:
          650 14px ui-sans-serif,
          system-ui,
          -apple-system,
          Segoe UI,
          Roboto;
      }
    </style>

    <text x="30" y="34" class="title ink"
      >Each rung adds one thing to the one below</text
    >

    <rect x="30" y="196" width="210" height="76" class="chip chip-state"></rect>
    <text x="135" y="220" text-anchor="middle" class="label ink"
      >Level 0 · Emitting</text
    >
    <text x="135" y="240" text-anchor="middle" class="small muted"
      >valid records, with as_of</text
    >
    <text x="135" y="256" text-anchor="middle" class="small muted"
      >kept apart from recorded_at</text
    >

    <line x1="240" y1="210" x2="268" y2="186" class="line dash"></line>

    <rect x="268" y="148" width="210" height="76" class="chip chip-state"
    ></rect>
    <text x="373" y="172" text-anchor="middle" class="label ink"
      >Level 1 · Append-only</text
    >
    <text x="373" y="192" text-anchor="middle" class="small muted"
      >nothing edited; every record</text
    >
    <text x="373" y="208" text-anchor="middle" class="small muted"
      >hashed and chained</text
    >

    <line x1="478" y1="162" x2="506" y2="138" class="line dash"></line>

    <rect x="506" y="100" width="210" height="76" class="chip chip-state"
    ></rect>
    <text x="611" y="124" text-anchor="middle" class="label ink"
      >Level 2 · Dependent</text
    >
    <text x="611" y="144" text-anchor="middle" class="small muted"
      >depends_on and invalidated_by</text
    >
    <text x="611" y="160" text-anchor="middle" class="small muted"
      >populated; discrepancies answered</text
    >

    <line x1="716" y1="114" x2="744" y2="90" class="line dash"></line>

    <rect x="744" y="52" width="210" height="76" class="chip chip-state"></rect>
    <text x="849" y="76" text-anchor="middle" class="label ink"
      >Level 3 · Contestable</text
    >
    <text x="849" y="96" text-anchor="middle" class="small muted"
      >standing declared; objections</text
    >
    <text x="849" y="112" text-anchor="middle" class="small muted"
      >answered within a clock</text
    >

    <text x="30" y="296" class="small muted">
      A system declares the highest level every record it emits satisfies, and a
      consumer reads that as a floor rather than a promise about any one record.
    </text>
    <text x="30" y="312" class="small muted">
      Declaring Level 0 honestly is conformance. Declaring Level 2 over a log
      that never populates invalidated_by is not.
    </text>
  </svg>
</figure>
